  "final_answer": "Fixed. The bug was in `OrderedMultiDict.addlist()`, which existed in two modules: `boltons/dictutils.py` and `boltons/urlutils.py` (the latter is a shadowed duplicate \u2014 the module re-imports the dictutils class at the end, but the local copy was still broken).\n\nThe old code did:\n```python\nif not v:\n    return\n...\nfor subv in v:\n    self_insert(k, subv)\nvalues.extend(v)\n```\nFor a one-shot iterator, the `for` loop consumed it, so `values.extend(v)` appended nothing \u2014 leaving the internal linked li",
